    "https://eodq.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX/job/3883": {
      "title": "On-Call Custodial Technician",
      "description": "Category: UPSEU Facilities JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Saratoga Springs, NY, United States This is an on call position. Can lead to fulltime if interested This is an on call position. Can lead to full time if interested Seeking a reliable and detail-oriented Custodial Technician (E-Tech) to join our facilities team. This position involves maintaining the cleanliness and safety of campus buildings through general and specialized cleaning tasks such as sweeping, mopping, vacuuming, dusting, restroom sanitation, trash removal, and event setup. Additional duties may include snow removal, minor maintenance, and handling recyclable or hazardous materials. Special assignments may include pool or recycling responsibilities. Must be comfortable using hand tools, cleaning equipment, and following safety protocols. Requirements: High school diploma or GED Basic math and reading comprehension Ability to lift up to 75 lbs. with assistance Valid driver's license may be required Pay: $20.72/hour per union contract; additional pay depending on assigned shift For questions about this opportunity, please feel free to contact Scott Wood at 518-580-5860 or scottwood@skidmore.edu Required documents needed to apply: On-line application Employment at Skidmore College is contingent upon an acceptable post-offer background check, physical and drug screening result. EEO STATEMENT Skidmore College is committed to being an inclusive campus community and, as an Equal Opportunity Employer, does not discriminate in its hiring or employment practices on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, gender, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, military or veteran status, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, predisposition or carrier status, domestic violence victim status, familial status, dating violence, or stalking, or any other category protected by applicable federal, state or local laws. Employment at Skidmore College is contingent upon an acceptable post-offer background check, physical and drug screening result. CREATIVE THOUGHT MATTERS. "
    },
    "https://eodq.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX/job/3878": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Economics and Asian Studies",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Saratoga Springs, NY, United States Skidmore College Assistant Professor, Economics and Asian Studies The Department of Economics at Skidmore College jointly with the Asian Studies Program invite applications for a tenure-track position at the assistant professor rank, beginning in the fall of 2027. This is the Frances Young Tang ’61 Professorship in Economics and Asian Studies. Applicants must possess a strong desire to teach and pursue research in a liberal arts environment in a department and program with a reputation for excellent teaching. The successful candidate will teach both electives and required courses in economics and Asian studies. Applicable JEL Fields: E [macroeconomics and monetary economics], O11 [Macroeconomic Analyses of Economic Development], O53 [Economywide country studies: Asia including middle east], P5 [Comparative Economic Systems], Z13 [Other special topics: Economic Sociology • Economic Anthropology • Language • Social and Economic Stratification] Summary: The Department of Economics at Skidmore College jointly with the Asian Studies Program invite applications for a tenure-track position at the assistant professor rank, beginning in the fall of 2027. This is the Frances Young Tang ’61 Professorship in Economics and Asian Studies. Applicants must possess a strong desire to teach and pursue research in a liberal arts environment in a department and program with a reputation for excellent teaching. The successful candidate will teach both electives and required courses in economics and Asian studies. Applicable JEL Fields: E [macroeconomics and monetary economics], O11 [Macroeconomic Analyses of Economic Development], O53 [Economywide country studies: Asia including middle east], P5 [Comparative Economic Systems], Z13 [Other special topics: Economic Sociology • Economic Anthropology • Language • Social and Economic Stratification] Responsibilities: Teach 18 credits per academic year in Economics and Asian Studies Contribute to interdisciplinary offerings such as the First-Year experience or relevant College general education programs Develop a coherent research stream and maintain a vigorous, ongoing research agenda that produces peer-reviewed publications in high-quality outlets. Advise students and participate in departmental service activities. Play a critical role in continuing to build the Asian Studies program through service. Qualifications: A minimum of a Ph.D. degree in Economics (advanced ABDs with dissertation defenses scheduled prior to the start of the fall semester 2027 will be considered). Research interest and teaching capability in economics and Asian studies relating to China and Asia. Evidence of teaching experience and promise and/or a teaching statement. Three reference letters are required as part of the application. One research paper to serve as evidence of scholarly promise is also required. Candidates should submit a cover letter explaining their ability to contribute in the areas described above, a curriculum vitae, one research paper, three letters of reference, a research statement, and a teaching statement and evidence of teaching capability. To learn more about and apply for this position please visit us online at: http://jobs.skidmore.edu Your cover letter should address the fields in which you are prepared to teach and how they relate to China and Asia. We will consider macroeconomists with an international orientation, specifically China and Asia. The college offers excellent research support. The standard teaching load is 18 credits per academic year (usually 5 courses per year, normally with 2 – 3 preps). New faculty receive a course release in their first year and are eligible for a pre-tenure sabbatical. Applications are due November 30. We will conduct first interviews in early to mid-January 2027. Salary Range: $95,000 - $105,000. Skidmore College offers a comprehensive benefits package. Our benefits plans provide choice and flexibility to support our employees' needs and those of their families. Benefits information: www.skidmore.edu/benefits About Skidmore College Skidmore is a highly selective liberal arts college that fosters creative approaches to teaching and learning. Skidmore’s faculty of teacher-scholars are devoted to the instruction and mentoring of approximately 2500 talented undergraduates. With its relatively small size and student-faculty ratio, the College is a close-knit academic community. Skidmore College is located in Saratoga Springs, NY which is recognized as a highly desirable place to live, based on the area’s rich history, safety, and access to recreation, culture, dining, and top-tier public schools. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Skidmore College is committed to being an inclusive campus community and, as an Equal Opportunity Employer, does not discriminate on the basis of gender, race, ethnicity, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, veteran or marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, domestic violence victim status, genetic information, prior arrest or conviction record, or any other category protected by law. Employment at Skidmore College is contingent upon an acceptable background check result. CREATIVE THOUGHT MATTERS. "
    },
    "https://eodq.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX/job/3879": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor,  GIS Center for Interdisciplinary Research",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Saratoga Springs, NY, United States Skidmore College invites applications for a full-time non-tenure track Assistant Teaching Professor position as manager of the GIS Center for Interdisciplinary Research beginning August 1, 2027. This is an initial 3-year appointment period and renewable. This position is 11-months per year. Summary: Skidmore College invites applications for a full-time non-tenure track Assistant Teaching Professor position as manager of the GIS Center for Interdisciplinary Research beginning August 1, 2027. This is an initial 3-year appointment period and renewable. This position is 11-months per year. Responsibilities : Teaches 3 sections of Introduction to GIS and one section of Advanced GIS Assists with the development of the GIS Center Supports faculty research and curriculum development Stewards the Center’s GIS software, data, and learning resources in partnership with relevant campus units. Qualifications : Master’s degree in GIS, geography, spatial data science, or related field required. Minimum of five years' experience in GIS, spatial analysis, or related field. Preferred : PhD in relevant field Experience teaching and mentoring undergraduate students Leadership and supervisory experience Competencies : Expertise in GIS technologies, spatial analysis, and data visualization Proficiency with ESRI and related GIS platforms Ability to collaborate across disciplines and build partnerships Excellent communication skills (presenting, training, consulting) Strategic thinking and program development capabilities Ability to translate complex technical concepts to diverse audiences Application Instructions : Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, and contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin on November 10, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Apply online: www.skidmore.edu/hr Questions? Please contact David Cohen, Associate Dean of the Faculty at dcohen1@skidmore.edu . Salary : $89,590 (increases based on the Collective Bargaining Agreement) Skidmore College offers a comprehensive benefits package. Our benefits plans provide choice and flexibility to support our employees' needs and those of their families. Benefits information: www.skidmore.edu/benefits All bargaining unit members shall be covered by a collective bargaining agreement between Skidmore College and Services Employees International Union (SEIU), Local 200 United. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of the Form I-9 and verification of identity and work authorization as required by federal law. Employment at Skidmore College is contingent upon an acceptable background check result. About Skidmore College Skidmore is a highly selective liberal arts college that fosters creative approaches to teaching and learning. Skidmore’s faculty of teacher-scholars are devoted to the instruction and mentoring of approximately 2500 talented undergraduates. With its relatively small size and student-faculty ratio, the College is a close-knit academic community. Skidmore College is located in Saratoga Springs, NY which is recognized as a highly desirable place to live, based on the area’s rich history, safety, and access to recreation, culture, dining, and top-tier public schools. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Skidmore College is committed to being an inclusive campus community and, as an Equal Opportunity Employer, does not discriminate on the basis of gender, race, ethnicity, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, veteran or marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, domestic violence victim status, genetic information, prior arrest or conviction record, or any other category protected by law. CREATIVE THOUGHT MATTERS. "
    },
    "https://eodq.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX/job/3861": {
      "title": "Riding Assistant/Instructor (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Category: Sports Instruction JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Saratoga Springs, NY, United States Summary The Department of Athletics, Fitness and Recreation at Skidmore College invites applications for a part-time Riding Assistant/Instructor in the College’s Riding Program. The Skidmore College Riding Program boasts a 9-time IHSA National Championship team. We teach Hunter Seat Equitation to college and community students at every level, from beginners to advanced jumping. Our program runs all year. We host IHSA and local competitions and we travel to USEF competitions in the summer. Our facility includes a 60-stall heated barn, a 200’ x 80’ indoor ring, a large outdoor ring, a horse walker, and 6 paddocks. We are looking for a motivated, organized, team oriented individual to join our team on a part-time basis. The position is all year, 25 hour per week. Hours are 8:30 - 1:30, Tuesday through Saturday. While we can be flexible with hours during the week, Saturdays are required. Responsibilities include but are not limited to the following: Longeing horses Leading horses to/from paddocks and horse walker Grooming horses Administering first aid Laundry Giving tours to prospective students When classes are in session, this position will drive College owned vehicle to/from campus to help facilitate students coming/going from classes. The ideal candidate will also be able to teach students classic hunter seat equitation from the absolute beginner through lower-level jumping. This is not a riding position, but riding opportunities may be available for the right candidate. Qualifications: A solid, practical foundation in horse care (grooming, tacking and untacking, longeing, hand walking, turning out, assisting students with tacking, untacking, and proper cooling out procedures, and basic equine first aid) is an absolute requirement as is a willing to adapt that knowledge to our way of doing things. Candidates must be ready to be in constant motion, have strong organizational and communication skills, be able to lift 50 pounds, and must have a valid driver’s license. Preferred Qualification: The ideal candidate will be able to teach beginning through novice jumping lessons with a thorough understanding of and ability to communicate effectively the fundamentals of Hunter Seat Equitation. Education: A college degree (2 or 4 year) with a minimum of three years of working in the hunter/jumper industry is required. Anticipated start date: November 1, 2026. Pay Range: $21 – 27 per hour commensurate with experience and ability to teach Required documents needed to apply: On-line application Cover Letter Resume List of Three References Employment at Skidmore College is contingent upon an acceptable post-offer background check result. No Visa Sponsorship is available for this position EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY STATEMENT Skidmore College is committed to being an inclusive campus community and, as an Equal Opportunity Employer, does not discriminate in its hiring or employment practices on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, gender, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, military or veteran status, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, predisposition or carrier status, domestic violence victim status, familial status, dating violence, or stalking, or any other category protected by applicable federal, state or local laws. CREATIVE THOUGHT MATTERS. "
    },
    "https://eodq.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX/job/3862": {
      "title": "Short Order Cook/Retail Dining Services",
      "description": "Category: UPSEU Dining Services JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Saratoga Springs, NY, United States Skidmore College Dining Services is accepting applications for the Short Order Cook / Retail Services. Job duties include but not limited to: Prepare, cook, serve, and clean work in dining areas, and perform other duties as described below or as assigned by the supervisor. Seeking a reliable and detail-oriented Short Order Cook/Retail Dining Services employee to join our Dining Services team. This position involves preparing, cooking, serving, and cleaning work and dining areas as well as greeting guests, checking IDs, selling guest tickets and completing sales on the POS system as assigned. Additional duties include stocking items for sale or service and cleaning the dining room and refrigerators, freezers, and all equipment used. Special assignments may include the dish room and special event/catering responsibilities. Must be comfortable using kitchen tools, cleaning equipment, and following safety protocols. Benefits: Skidmore College offers employees generous benefits including health insurance plans, paid time off and holiday pay, a retirement savings plan, tuition benefits for employees and their dependents, paid medical leave, paid training, free CDTA bus pass, campus dining discounts, free parking, free athletic center access, and more! Requirements: High school diploma or GED Basic math and reading comprehension Ability to lift up to 30 lbs. with appropriate equipment and assistance SERV Safe Food Handler/HACCP Certified within one year of employment Willingness to attend training and work weekends/overtime as needed Pay: $20.72/hour per union contract; additional pay depending on assigned shift Hours: 40 hours per week Academic Work Schedule Saturday 5:00pm - 1:30 am Sunday 2:30pm -11:00pm Monday off Tuesday 2:30pm - 11:00pm Wednesday off Thursday 2:30 pm - 11:00pm Saturday 5:00pm - 1:30 am For questions about this opportunity, please feel free to contact John Everett at 518-580-5844 or jeverett@skidmore.edu . Required documents needed to apply: On-line application Employment at Skidmore College is contingent upon an acceptable post-offer background check and physical and drug screening result. EEO STATEMENT Skidmore College is committed to being an inclusive campus community and, as an Equal Opportunity Employer, does not discriminate in its hiring or employment practices on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, gender, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, military or veteran status, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, predisposition or carrier status, domestic violence victim status, familial status, dating violence, or stalking, or any other category protected by applicable federal, state or local laws. CREATIVE THOUGHT MATTERS. "
