    "https://eodq.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX/job/3847": {
      "title": "Health & Human Physiological Sciences Faculty Position (Tenure-Track, Open Rank)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Saratoga Springs, NY, United States Health & Human Physiological Sciences Faculty Position (Tenure-Track, Open Rank) Summary The Health and Human Physiological Sciences (HHPS) Department invites applications for a full-time open-rank tenure-track faculty position in HHPS to begin in the fall of 2027. The HHPS Department is located in the recently opened Billie Tisch Center for Integrated Sciences, a state-of-the-art teaching and research facility that fosters unique interdisciplinary connections across the sciences. The HHPS Department has a suite of laboratories for conducting sophisticated, in-depth research from the molecular/cellular level to applied physiology in animal and human models. Our suite of laboratories allows for research interests across a breadth of areas including environmental/occupational physiology, cardiovascular physiology, endocrinology, and metabolism. Responsibilities include undergraduate teaching within the department and as part of the College’s first-year experience program; developing and implementing a research program that involves undergraduates and competes for national grants (e.g., NIH-AIREA); advising/mentoring students; and serving the department, the college, and broader profession. Applicants should embrace the teacher-scholar model and demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and mentoring within a liberal arts environment. Candidates should have expertise in exercise physiology or a closely related area of human physiology and health, with the potential to contribute to courses across the HHPS curriculum. Areas of scholarly interest may include, but are not limited to, exercise physiology, integrative physiology, physical activity and health, nutrition, or other biomedical and health-related fields. Candidates should demonstrate the potential to develop an active and sustainable research program that meaningfully engages undergraduate students in the research process. We particularly value candidates who view teaching and scholarship as complementary activities and who are enthusiastic about mentoring students as developing scientists and health professionals. Experience in teaching, postdoctoral research, and pursuit of extramural funding are highly desirable. We are seeking an energetic teacher/scholar who embraces interdisciplinary work in a creative and supportive environment. We are expressly interested in faculty with expertise in exercise physiology, broadly, and/or areas complementary to existing faculty expertise in the department. Responsibilities Teach 18 contact hours per academic year (~5 classes) including: Introduction to Exercise Physiology, Human Anatomy & Physiology, Research Techniques in Human Physiology/Exercise Testing and Prescription, Human Nutrition, Advanced Exercise Physiology, Research Design, and special topics upper-level courses. Responsibilities will also include occasionally teaching a first-year seminar course in the College’s first-year experience seminar course. Conduct and disseminate research with HHPS students. Pursue funding through governmental, professional organizations, and/or industry partners. Dissemination of research through presentations at scientific conferences and publications in peer-reviewed journals. Act in service to the department, college, and broader professional community. This is a 9-month per academic year position with benefits eligibility and salary paid over 12-months per year. Qualifications A Ph.D. or similar degree in the area of exercise/applied physiology/kinesiology or a related field (ABD considered). Preference will be given to candidates with undergraduate teaching experience, postdoctoral fellowship experience, active research agendas, and those with experience in pursuing extramural research funding. Salary: $80,000 - $120,000 depending on rank. Skidmore College offers a comprehensive benefits package, including a relocation stipend and a lab startup package. Tenure-track faculty (assistant professors) are eligible for a pre-tenure research leave in their fourth year at the college. Our benefits plans provide choice and flexibility to support our employees' needs and those of their families. Benefits information: www.skidmore.edu/benefits Application Instructions: Applicants should submit the following materials to the HR application portal: A cover letter outlining your interest and ability to fulfill the position outlined above Curriculum vitae A teaching statement that outlines your experience and describes your teaching style, instructional techniques, and general pedagogical approach. A research statement outlining your research experience and goals, including potential avenues to pursue funding. Contact information for 3 professional references Applications will be reviewed starting October 30 th 2026. Apply online: www.skidmore.edu/hr Questions? Please contact Steve Ives, Professor and Chair of Health & Human Physiological Sciences, sives@skidmore.edu or T.H. Reynolds, Professor and Associate Chair of Health & Human Physiological Sciences, treynold@skidmore.edu About Skidmore College : Skidmore is a highly selective liberal arts college that fosters creative approaches to teaching and learning. Skidmore’s faculty of teacher-scholars are devoted to the instruction and mentoring of approximately 2500 talented undergraduates. With its relatively small size and student-faculty ratio, the College is a close-knit academic community situated in a beautiful and historic setting. Employment at Skidmore College is contingent upon an acceptable post-offer background check result. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Skidmore College is committed to being an inclusive campus community and, as an Equal Opportunity Employer, does not discriminate in its hiring or employment practices on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, gender, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, military or veteran status, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, predisposition or carrier status, domestic violence victim status, familial status, dating violence, or stalking, or any other category protected by applicable federal, state or local laws. CREATIVE THOUGHT MATTERS. "
    },
    "https://eodq.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX/job/3851": {
      "title": "Assistant Lecturer, World Languages and Literatures",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: United States The Department of World Languages and Literatures at Skidmore College invites applications for a part-time, non-tenure track Assistant Lecturer position in Chinese beginning January 2027. This is a one semester appointment. Responsibilities: Teach one 4-credit Chinese Language course in the spring 2027 semester. A minimum of an MA in Chinese linguistics, language pedagogy, second-language acquisition or a related field; native or near-native proficiency in Chinese and excellent command of English; and evidence of experience and commitment to language teaching at all levels typically offered in U.S. universities and college Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the college level Salary Range: $10,228.00 All bargaining unit members shall be covered by a collective bargaining agreement between Skidmore College and Services Employees International Union (SEIU), Local 200 United. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, and contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin on October 10 th and continue until the position is filled. Apply online: https://www.skidmore.edu/hr/index.php Questions? Please contact Mao Chen, Professor of Chinese , maochen@skidmore.edu About Skidmore College Skidmore is a highly selective liberal arts college of ~2,500 students representing 47 states and 46 countries. With a student faculty ratio of 8:1, we value close interaction, creative pedagogy, and teacher scholar excellence. Employment at Skidmore College is contingent upon an acceptable post-offer background check result. No Visa Sponsorship is available for this position EEO STATEMENT Skidmore College is committed to being an inclusive campus community and, as an Equal Opportunity Employer, does not discriminate in its hiring or employment practices on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, gender, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, military or veteran status, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, predisposition or carrier status, domestic violence victim status, familial status, dating violence, or stalking, or any other category protected by applicable federal, state or local laws. CREATIVE THOUGHTMATTERS. "
    },
    "https://eodq.fa.us6.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX/job/3816": {
      "title": "On-Call Testing Coordinator",
      "description": "Category: Student Services JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Saratoga Springs, NY, United States Summary Skidmore College’s Learning Commons is seeking dependable, organized individuals to provide on-call support in the Testing Center during busy testing periods, including midterms, final exams, and other high-volume days throughout the semester. This is a flexible, on-call position with no regular weekly schedule. Hours are based on Testing Center needs. The position may be especially appealing to retired educators or others interested in occasional work in a college setting. Primary Job Duties checking students in and out of exams, preparing and managing testing materials, monitoring testing rooms, and helping maintain a quiet, organized testing environment. Qualifications Education: Two years of college or the equivalent of an Associate’s degree, along with experience working in a setting where organization, accuracy, and attention to detail are important. Experience: Experience in education, student services, testing, or administrative support is preferred. The position requires strong attention to detail, reliability, sound judgment, and the ability to handle confidential information appropriately. Salary: $18.00 per hour Required documents needed to apply: On-line application Cover Letter Resume Employment at Skidmore College is contingent upon an acceptable post-offer background check result. No Visa Sponsorship is available for this position EEO STATEMENT Skidmore College is committed to being an inclusive campus community and, as an Equal Opportunity Employer, does not discriminate in its hiring or employment practices on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, gender, age, national or ethnic origin, physical or mental disability, military or veteran status, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, predisposition or carrier status, domestic violence victim status, familial status, dating violence, or stalking, or any other category protected by applicable federal, state or local laws. CREATIVE THOUGHT MATTERS. "
    },
